                  <provenance type="#m"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem. </orgName><p>Cambridge, Emmanuel Coll.
                        35, Trinity Coll. 345, and the Hilton in Philadelphia contain notes in the
                        hand of James Grenehalgh (professed 1495, see H. E. Allen). Grenehalgh also
                        annotated Bodleian, Douce 262 (see under London, Charterhouse), BL, Royal 5
                        A.v (see under Coventry, Charterhouse) and his monogram is in BL, Add. 24461
                        and 37790 and probably Harley 2373 (see under Mount Grace).</p><p>The
                        character of the notes in this copy suggest that Greenhalgh owned
                     it.</p></provenance>
